The other day, my Valk was wandering through the quest, looking for
Lord Surtur's cave, when a trapdoor opened up beneath her--dropping her
straight into a lava level.  She cleared out the immediate threats, and
went up the stairs--finding herself in the middle of the cave, fire
ants and giants rushing towards her.  Despite having to pop back down
the stairs at one point to heal up, she was able to fight her way free.
 Having picked up a decent amount of loot from the melee, she decided
to go back to the Norn's chest rather than continue on down.

After stashing her loot, she hiked back to the cave--where she got the
typical "...This then is the entrance to the cave of Surtur. It looks
like you're not going to get in without a fight though."  Which
surprised her (and me), because everything was dead already...it looked
like she could walk right on in, and so she did.

Incidentally, Lord Surtur died in two hits, which was another
(pleasant) surprise, but mostly unrelated to my question.

Is this a bug?  Since the locate levels have undiggable floors,
shouldn't trapdoors/holes from the upper filler levels not drop you
below them?  If I had just continued down and killed Lord Surtur, then
climbed back up above the locate level, would I have gotten the locate
message if I went back to it, since that would've been the first time I
went down to the locate level?

